  "spec": "DESIGN.md — installations, the machine seam, standalone save cards (issue #181)",
  "description": "PPSSPP's savedata answer where the question names a PSP disc: the disc's DISC_ID read (atlas/psp_disc.py) and the SAVEDATA folders beginning with it stated as the game's save unit, own-folders-by-prefix — or the save_id hole where the id or the folders are not established.",
  "vectors": [
    {
      "name": "ppsspp-names-the-discs-savedata-folders-by-its-id",
      "rationale": "The question names a plain ISO whose PSP_GAME/PARAM.SFO states DISC_ID ULUS10064 — the id PPSSPP loads for the disc (PSPLoaders.cpp:129-141 at ppsspp v1.20.4). SAVEDATA holds two games' folders: ULUS10064DATA00 (a savedata PARAM.SFO, carrying SAVEDATA_FILE_LIST and SAVEDATA_PARAMS), ULUS10064SETTINGS (no PARAM.SFO, which an install always writes, so no install), ULUS10064INSTALL (a PARAM.SFO with neither savedata key — a game-data install, PSPGamedataInstallDialog.cpp:211-243 — left out), ULES00001DATA (another game's), and a file ULUS10064.txt (no folder). The answer states the unit own-folders-by-prefix with prefix ULUS10064 and the two save folders as members, needs empty.",
